    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0882" n="864" xml:id="pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/10–2)46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Durbrow</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-17T16:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1844. Dept’s 1651 Sept 13. Pls inform FonOff French Govt has now replied
                    favorably re abolition Alcorn Italy<anchor n="57" xml:id="d580-f1"/> and Dept is
                    therefore anxious obtain FonOff reply soonest possible.<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d580-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="57" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 4933, October 2, from Paris, conveyed the message of the French
                    favorable reply (740.00119 Control (Italy)/10–246).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d580-f2" n="58" xml:id="d580-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 3906, October 19, from Moscow, Mr. Durbrow reported that on October
                    17 he had sent a letter to Dekanozov giving the substance of this telegram. On
                    October 18 he was told that the matter was under consideration and that a
                    decision could be expected soon. (740.00119 Control (Italy)/10–1946)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
